Border-aware (masked) AKAZE descriptors: the variant of docs/FINAL_RUN.md
item 0c that was evaluated against the 20 px replicate pad and not kept
(owner kept pad 20, 2026-11-02). Kept here so the 0c numbers can be
reproduced; it is not on the libfprint sift-matcher branch.

Adds to libfprint (fpi-keypoint-akaze.[ch], fpi-keypoint-match.[ch]):
fpi_akaze_detect_full(), fpi_akaze_extract_masked(),
fpi_akaze_match_score_masked(), fpi_keypoint_match_score_masked(),
FPI_AKAZE_DESCRIPTOR_BITS / _MIN_VALID_BITS / _MASKED_BORDER, the masks
and valid_bits fields of FpiAkazeFeatures, and the tests
/keypoint/akaze-masked, /keypoint/masked-distance, /keypoint/masked-score.
The default (padded) path is unchanged: the same scores with or without it.

Apply it to a copy of a sift-matcher tree whose AKAZE files carry no masked
code, rebuild the bench library from that copy, and run with the masked
knobs:

  cp -a ~/Repo/FingerPrintReader/libfprint-upstream ~/lf-masked
  patch -d ~/lf-masked -p1 < akaze/masked.patch
  (cd ~/lf-masked && meson setup _b && ninja -C _b && meson test -C _b)
  LIBFPRINT=~/lf-masked akaze/build.sh lib
  # best masked row of 0c: floor first, border 2, floor 243
  FPBENCH_AKAZE_MASK=1 FPBENCH_AKAZE_BORDER=2 FPBENCH_AKAZE_MIN_BITS=243 \
  FPBENCH_AKAZE_FLOOR_FIRST=1 PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1 python3 bench/big_eval.py \
    --matcher akaze_c --data <datasets> --out <dir>

Other 0c rows: drop FPBENCH_AKAZE_FLOOR_FIRST, or vary FPBENCH_AKAZE_BORDER
(1-3) and FPBENCH_AKAZE_MIN_BITS (120-405). Without the patch the masked
knobs stop with an error naming this file. akaze/build.sh lib rebuilds
libakaze_c.so in place: run it again on the unpatched tree afterwards to
get the default library back. (git apply works as well as patch -p1.)

